{"id":"VHH__tool__noise3d_direction","collection":"VHH","category":"tool","source_path":"VHH/tool/noise3d_direction.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::noise3d_direction"],"counts":{"nodes":32,"connections":68,"values":24,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Direction Field - One of the pre-made fields. This is a simple field for changing the direction of the displacement. Noise may be added to it","documentation_search":"noise3d direction Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Direction Field - One of the pre-made fields. This is a simple field for changing the direction of the displacement. Noise may be added to it Input direction The vector of the direction you wish to use. mask Scalar field mask on the outgoing field. warp vector field Domain warp on the outgoing field. add noise When checked, a fractal turbulence is added to the direction based on the settings below. magnitude The magnitude of the noise. num frequencies This is the total number of noise frequencies to sum. Generally as this number increases there will be more detail or small scale noise. The value does not need to be an integer. frequency This is the base frequency of the fractal noise. Higher values have finer detail. frequency ratio This is the ratio of each noise frequency to the previous. ratio This is the ratio of magnitude of each noise frequency to the previous. If it is the same as frequency ratio then the magnitude of each noise will be the same relative to its scale. time A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. seed The seed to use for randomization. translate Move the field. rotate Rotate the field. scale Scale the field. invert mask Inverts the scalar field mask. adjust mask A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask. warp amount The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp. Output turbulence field The field result ready to be used.","port_names":["add_noise","adjust_mask","direction","frequency","frequency_ratio","invert_mask","magnitude","mask","num_frequencies","ratio","rotate","scale","seed","time","translate","turbulence_field","warp_amount","warp_vector_field"],"node_types_search":["Core::Conversion::degrees_to_radians","Core::Fields::advect_field","Core::Fields::fcurve_field","Core::Fields::field_is_empty","Core::Fields::fractal_turbulence_field","Core::Fields::scalar_field","Core::Fields::transform_field","Core::Fields::vector_field","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::clamp","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::euler_to_quaternion","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::subtract","change_range_field","maskWerks"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::noise3d_direction","uri_imported":"stream:/stream","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/noise3d_direction.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Warp"}]},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/noise3d_direction.md","documentation":"### ***noise3d_direction***\n<font size = 1>**Component Compound** - this compound is a component in the the *displacer* ecosystem.<br /><br /></font>\n<font size = 2>**Direction Field** - One of the pre-made fields.  This is a simple field for changing the direction of the displacement.  Noise may be added to it</font><br />\n\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***direction***</span>\n<br />The vector of the direction you wish to use.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***mask***</span>\n<br />Scalar field mask on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***warp_vector_field***</span>\n<br />Domain warp on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***add_noise***</span>\n<br />When checked, a fractal turbulence is added to the direction based on the settings below.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***magnitude***</span>\n<br />The magnitude of the noise.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***num_frequencies***</span>\n<br />This is the total number of noise frequencies to sum. Generally as this number increases there will be more detail or small scale noise. The value does not need to be an integer.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency***</span>\n<br />This is the base frequency of the fractal noise. Higher values have finer detail.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency_ratio***</span>\n<br />This is the ratio of each noise frequency to the previous.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***ratio***</span>\n<br />This is the ratio of magnitude of each noise frequency to the previous. If it is the same as frequency_ratio then the magnitude of each noise will be the same relative to its scale.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***time***</span>\n<br />A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. \n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***seed***</span>\n<br />The seed to use for randomization.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***translate***</span>\n<br />Move the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***rotate***</span>\n<br />Rotate the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***scale***</span>\n<br />Scale the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_mask***</span>\n<br />Inverts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_mask***</span>\n<br />A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***warp_amount***</span>\n<br />The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp.\n\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***turbulence_field***</span>\n<br />The field result ready to be used.","ports":[{"name":"magnitude","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.100000001f"},{"name":"num_frequencies","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"6f"},{"name":"frequency","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"1f"},{"name":"ratio","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.5f"},{"name":"frequency_ratio","direction